Z||000006||Pontiaddict||10-23-2001||01:34 AM||||Actually, (I found this out last year when Michigan was infested with them.) the bugs that most people are hiving a problem with aren't ladybugs at all, they're actually an asian beetle that farmers realesed for one reason or another to control something. These beetles have a wierd pattern of dots on them, (some don't have any spots at all) they usually have white spots on their head (or maybe it was that they don't have any spots on their head) and they bite people. (the easiest way to tell)<P>I'd give you more info, but as you can tell, my memory isn't the greatest anymore.||||reg||1
