Z||000015||Old Lar||10-23-2001||11:12 AM||||The ladybug infestation is from them looking for a place to hibernate for the winter.  The weather had been warm, then a cold front came through, the bugs started looking for a warm place.  They appeared on the south walls of buildings around here.  They are really beneficial insects that control aphids on plants. Rather them or lots of pesticides?<P>It happens almost yearly, but they came out all at once or so it seemed.||||reg||1
