Z||000019||Elvira||10-23-2001||01:45 PM||||Don't feel bad, we are in the same boat up here in NH, but theyare protected up here.  It is illegal to kill them.  They say to vacuum them up, but make sure you put bubble wrap in the vacuum so you don't kill them.  I say to heck with that, there are literally hundreds of them.  UNH cross-bred ladybugs with something elso for an experiment, then when they were done, they released them so now there are all these hybrid ladybugs of various wierd color schemes flying around.  On a better note, at least they aren't roaches!!<P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||1
Z||000020||Return of Fiero||10-23-2001||01:54 PM||||might as wall be roaches, the dang things are eating my screes, i have to use the a/c in the house at night, and the nights are below 50. i left the window open 5 nights ago, and the next night, there were lady bugs everywhere. looking to my right, i see my screen has many holes (about 3 dozen) around the size of bic pen is around. they also are eating my pumpkins!!! they must have been breeding lady bugs with roaches, or maybe with ants. you close to the collage, could you go ask them?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Myke||||reg||1
Z||000021||btoth||10-23-2001||02:44 PM||||The freakin' yellow ones are everywhere!! I've two flying around in here now.  They keep bitting my mom but they just land on me and I take them outside.  I don't know what's up with the crazy lady bugs this year.  Oh, and I guess they're supposed to stink if you squish 'em.  Hmm.<P>But what I really hate are the stupid spiders we have.  Creepy, inch long black spiders.  You kill one, and the next day there's another one.  Always on the ceiling too, like they're hunting you.  And you try to kill them <P>*lady bug landed on me... hold on...*<P>and you just know you're going to miss and the spider is going to fall on your head or something and then it'll crawl around on you and you'll never find it.  I have yet to actually see any webs or egg sacks around the house, they must be breeding under my bed or something... eeewww.  I wish we just had tarantulas or something big that I could see and couldn't sneek up on you out of no where... of course, you can't just go killing a big spider like that with a kleenex either.||||reg||1
